{
  "qualification": "service-manifest-derived-id-limit",
  "contract": "service-manifest",
  "contract_version": 1,
  "description": "Producer-derived boundary cases for the post-default resource ID limit that Alloy's ServiceManifest::validate() applies outside the service-manifest v1 schema (ferrum-contracts#80). Every case is valid against schemas/service-manifest/v1.schema.json (schema_valid); producer_exports records whether the owner's validate() and export accept it. A schema check alone does not establish that a manifest is exportable. Each derived_resource_ids entry is a resource ID Alloy's export generates from the proxy ID (Alloy's tests call these generated_ids); producer_exports is true exactly when every entry is at most edge_resource_id_max_length characters. The cases start from fixtures/service-manifest/valid/plain-http.json and change only gateway: an explicit 241- or 242-character proxy_id, correlation_id false, and, without an exporter, no otel_endpoint or otel_root_sampling_ratio. plain-http.json has no health check, so no -upstream ID is generated. A proxy ID defaulted from service.name is at most 63 characters and cannot reach this boundary.",
  "edge_resource_id_max_length": 254,
  "producer": {
    "repo": "ferrum-edge/ferrum-alloy",
    "ref": "main",
    "commit": "db412da37564ffbe869e2b40530dbebf5afe7ac8",
    "availability": "unreleased",
    "paths": [
      "crates/ferrum-alloy-edge/src/manifest.rs",
      "crates/ferrum-alloy-edge/src/export.rs",
      "crates/ferrum-alloy-edge/tests/export.rs"
    ],
    "symbols": [
      "EDGE_RESOURCE_ID_MAX_LENGTH",
      "ServiceManifest::validate",
      "export::resources",
      "OTEL_TRACING_PLUGIN_ID_SUFFIX",
      "each_generated_id_suffix_is_checked_at_its_boundary",
      "the_trace_plugin_bounds_a_proxy_id_without_other_derived_resources"
    ],
    "note": "Since ferrum-alloy#313 the export always generates the <proxy_id>-otel-tracing plugin, with or without gateway.otel_endpoint, and validate() bounds its ID by EDGE_RESOURCE_ID_MAX_LENGTH (254, Edge's MAX_ID_LENGTH in src/config/types.rs). The cases transcribe the propagation-only and otel families of each_generated_id_suffix_is_checked_at_its_boundary (241 accepted, 242 refused with an error naming -otel-tracing). Unchanged on Alloy main at 0e8a96a24c149432f0c3583732d8a3875db756ce."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "no-exporter-241",
      "description": "No health check, correlation disabled and no gateway.otel_endpoint. Alloy still generates the otel_tracing plugin (it removes a caller's trace context), so the 241-character proxy ID derives a 254-character plugin ID, at Edge's limit. Alloy exports it.",
